      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Execute the rigidity experiment by running the Python script that implements the numerical scan for the selected \"Universal Approximation Saturation\" hypothesis. The script will sweep the number of training constraints (w) and measure the minimal hidden width (N_c) required to achieve zero violation (max absolute error ≤ 1e-3) on held-out points. This directly tests whether N_c(w) plateaus (rigid) or grows unbounded (fat)."
    },
